# Non-secret runtime config for the `nfe` Cloud Functions codebase.
#
# ⚠️ THE ONE DELIBERATE EXCEPTION to the repo's one-root-`.env.example` convention
# (#730), carved out in packages/config-eslint/rules/env-example-location.test.js.
# Every OTHER app-level copy was consolidated into the repo-root file because apps
# load the repo-root `.env.local`. This one is a different mechanism entirely: its
# target is `apps/nfe/functions/.env` — the DEPLOY-TIME runtime env of a nested,
# non-workspace Cloud Functions codebase that the repo-root `.env.local` never
# reaches. Documenting these names in the root file would tell you to put them
# somewhere they do nothing.
#
# Copy this to `apps/nfe/functions/.env` (gitignored). `prepare-deploy.mjs` copies
# `.env*` (except `.env.local` / `.env.example`) into the deploy artifact, and
# firebase loads them as the function's runtime env at deploy.
#
#  - SECRETS (NFE_CERT_ENC_KEY / NFE_CERT_BASE64 / NFE_CERT_PASSWORD) do NOT go
#    here — set them with `firebase functions:secrets:set <NAME>`.
#  - FIREBASE_* names are reserved by Firebase and cannot be set via .env (the
#    admin SDK uses ADC + defaults the database id to `default`).

# Env-fallback A1 (test): a filial with no uploaded cert signs with the env A1.
NFE_CERT_ENV_FALLBACK=1

# Optional — these default to homologacao / SP in runtime.ts:
# NFE_AMBIENTE=homologacao
# NFE_UF=SP

# Produção only — the sweep's EPEC branch signs + emits:
# NFE_ALLOW_PRODUCAO=true

# Optional — the reconciliarNfe queue region (defaults to the function's own region):
# NFE_TASKS_REGION=us-east1
